# See https://docs.github.com/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files for more about ignoring files.

# The repository is laid out as `frontend/` (the Vue + PixiJS game, which Vite builds and Vitest tests),
# `backend/` (the Go server that holds the chat and the tapes), `docs/`, `tools/`, and `assets-source/`:
# everything in this file is a path inside one of those.

# Compiled output
/frontend/dist
/tmp
/tmp-smoke*
/tmp-compare*
/tmp-probe*
/tmp-patch*

# Scratch a session leaves at the root — a dump it read once, a conversion script, a tar of what it
# dumped: nothing of it is anybody's source, and a session should not have to think about it before
# committing (`tmp-smoke*/`, `tmp-probe*/` and the like are already above).
/tmp-*

# The server's own build, and whatever its database and tapes are pointed at: a running server's chat is
# a SQLite file and a tape is a file per session, and neither is anybody's source.
/backend/garden-server
/backend/garden-server.exe
/backend/tmp
/backend/data
/data

# Scratch images dumped into the served assets under their own hash, which is nobody's asset:
# `bg.png`, `box/box.png` and the character folders are the only things that belong there.
/frontend/public/assets/[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]*.png

# Recordings saved from the game's own debug panel, which land in `frontend/tests/records/`: half a minute of a run is a
# few hundred kilobytes of JSON, and nine tenths of it is the two debug tracks. `frontend/tests/records/README.md` says how
# they are read and stays tracked, so the folder is there in a fresh clone and says what it is for; `git add -f`
# takes one recording in if it is ever wanted.
/frontend/tests/records/*
!/frontend/tests/records/README.md

# Node
# The game's own dependencies live beside its `package.json`; the tools at the repository's root
# (`tools/smoke.mjs`, `tools/check-textures.mjs`, the `ruffle-*` and `probe-*` scripts) resolve `puppeteer`
# and Ruffle from a root `node_modules`, which is where `npm i --no-save puppeteer @ruffle-rs/ruffle` puts them.
/node_modules
/frontend/node_modules
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log

# IDEs and editors
.idea/
.project
.classpath
.c9/
*.launch
.settings/
*.sublime-workspace

# The coding agent's own per-session state (ZCode)
.zcode/

# Visual Studio Code
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.history/*

# Miscellaneous
.sass-cache/
/connect.lock
/coverage
/libpeerconnection.log
testem.log
/typings

# System files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
